---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro"
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro"
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro"
import { getRelativeLocaleUrl } from "astro:i18n"
import ArrowRightIcon from "../../assets/icons/arrow-right.svg"

const lang = Astro.currentLocale || "en"
---

<Layout
  title="About the project | 100cosas.dev"
  description="Learn the mission behind 100cosas.dev: a practical collection of software fundamentals to become a better programmer, one tip at a time."
  canonical="/en/about-the-project/"
  alternateUrl="/sobre-el-proyecto/"
>
  <Navbar alternateUrl="/sobre-el-proyecto/" />

  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="flex-grow w-full max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-14 md:pt-24 pb-28">
    <header class="max-w-3xl mb-16 md:mb-24">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal mb-6 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="size-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
        100cosas.dev
      </p>
      <h1 class="reveal font-serif font-normal text-5xl md:text-7xl leading-[1.02] tracking-[-0.03em] text-fg mb-8" style="--i: 1">
        About the <em class="italic">project</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="reveal font-serif text-xl md:text-2xl leading-snug text-fg-dim text-pretty max-w-2xl" style="--i: 2">
        An initiative by <a
            href="https://midu.dev"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            aria-label="midudev website (opens in a new tab)"
            class="text-fg underline decoration-accent/40 decoration-1 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent transition-colors">midudev</a> to strengthen the foundations of software development.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-16 md:space-y-20">
      <section class="about-section">
        <div>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-accent tabular-nums">01</span>
          <h2 class="font-serif font-normal text-2xl md:text-[1.75rem] leading-tight tracking-[-0.015em] text-fg mt-2 text-balance">Why this book?</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="about-body">
          <p>
            This book was born out of the need to collect and modernize
            fundamental advice for programmers. It is inspired by the collective
            work <strong>"97 Things Every Programmer Should Know"</strong>,
            updating its spirit with the most relevant lessons from modern development.
          </p>
          <p>
            The goal is to offer a roadmap of knowledge that transcends specific
            programming languages and frameworks.
            Tips that will be just as valid today as they will be in ten years.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <div>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-accent tabular-nums">02</span>
          <h2 class="font-serif font-normal text-2xl md:text-[1.75rem] leading-tight tracking-[-0.015em] text-fg mt-2 text-balance">What will you find here?</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="about-body">
          <p>This is not just a list of advice; it is a tool to:</p>
          <ul class="about-list">
            <li><strong>Reflect</strong> on the daily practice of programming.</li>
            <li><strong>Discover</strong> design and architecture principles that are often overlooked.</li>
            <li><strong>Internalize</strong> concepts that will make you a better professional, one tip at a time.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <div>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-accent tabular-nums">03</span>
          <h2 class="font-serif font-normal text-2xl md:text-[1.75rem] leading-tight tracking-[-0.015em] text-fg mt-2 text-balance">Programming in the AI era</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="about-body">
          <p>
            We live in an era where Artificial Intelligence can generate code in
            seconds. However, this makes
            <strong>having solid foundations more important than ever</strong>.
          </p>

          <blockquote class="about-quote">
            Why? Because AI is a tool, not a substitute for professional judgment.
          </blockquote>

          <p>
            Understanding the "why" behind the code, knowing when a solution is
            scalable, detecting code smells, and applying robust design principles
            is what allows a programmer to guide the AI, rather than being guided
            by it.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Foundations are the basis that allow you to discern if what the AI
            generates is really the best solution for your problem.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-line p-6 sm:p-10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6 sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
        <div class="max-w-md">
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-fg mb-2">Ready to start?</h2>
          <p class="font-serif text-lg text-fg-dim leading-snug">Explore all 100 tips, track your progress and become a better programmer one step at a time.</p>
        </div>
        <a
          href={getRelativeLocaleUrl(lang, "/")}
          class="group shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-fg text-bg px-5 py-2.5 text-[13px] font-medium hover:opacity-85 transition-opacity self-start sm:self-auto"
        >
          View tips
          <ArrowRightIcon class="size-3.5 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5" stroke-width="1.6" />
        </a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .about-section {
      grid-template-columns: 240px minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 3rem;
    }
  }

  .about-body {
    max-width: 38rem;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-body);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .about-body > * + * {
    margin-top: 1.1em;
  }

  .about-body strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .about-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6em;
  }

  .about-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.5em;
  }

  .about-list li::before {
    content: "—";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .about-quote {
    margin: 1.6em 0 !important;
    padding-left: 1.25em;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.35em;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
